text: Copy selections exactly and keep fractional line heights

- Copying a window text selection no longer trims it. Indentation, a lone
  tab and selected spaces are text. Copying only whitespace used to write
  nothing, leaving the previous clipboard contents in place.
- SelectableText::paint_selection is public, so virtualized plain-text
  views can paint selections with the same wrapped-line geometry.
- Inputs keep fractional line heights. Layout, hit testing, scrolling and
  painting share one value instead of rounding every row.

Remove when upstream copies selections verbatim and keeps fractional rows.

diff --git a/src/input/editor.rs b/src/input/editor.rs
index f69d6de..1fd0c5a 100644
--- a/src/input/editor.rs
+++ b/src/input/editor.rs
@@ -225,7 +225,8 @@ mod tests {
     #[gpui::test]
     fn the_rows_follow_the_font_size(cx: &mut TestAppContext) {
         // With nothing set, the theme's monospace size, not the ambient one.
-        assert_eq!(line_height(cx, None), px(20.));
+        // Rows keep the fractional line height rather than rounding to 20px.
+        assert_eq!(line_height(cx, None), px(19.5));
         // A text style set on the editor refines over that, rows and all.
         assert_eq!(line_height(cx, Some(px(24.))), px(36.));
         assert_eq!(line_height(cx, Some(px(40.))), px(60.));
